# The simulator writes its configuration next to wherever it is started from.
# The root .gitignore already covers the ordinary build output, so only the
# files this simulator generates are listed here.
#
# There used to be exceptions below these, keeping the copies in the simulator's
# own folder "for testing". They named opssat-spacecraft-simulator, a directory
# renamed to cubesat- long ago, so they never matched anything and those files
# were never tracked. They are not reinstated here: the files hold machine
# local state, such as which port Celestia listens on and how fast the
# simulation runs, and belong to whoever ran the simulator rather than to the
# repository.
**/_SIMULATOR-header.txt
**/_SIMULATOR-templates.txt
**/_SIMULATOR-scheduler.txt
**/_SIMULATOR-filter.txt
**/_SIMULATOR-scheduler_backup*.txt

# The names these had before the simulator stopped being OPS-SAT's alone. The
# simulator renames them on its next run, so these lines only matter between
# updating and running it once. They go when the renaming does, at v6.0.
**/_OPS-SAT-SIMULATOR-header.txt
**/_OPS-SAT-SIMULATOR-templates.txt
**/_OPS-SAT-SIMULATOR-scheduler.txt
**/_OPS-SAT-SIMULATOR-filter.txt
**/_OPS-SAT-SIMULATOR-scheduler_backup*.txt

# Written to the working directory by the simulator when the platform
# configuration changes. The other two modules that produce it ignore it in the
# same way; this module did not, which is how a copy full of one developer's
# absolute paths came to be committed.
**/platformsim.properties
